# Opinion

Meeting: 0002-bootstrap-rps-arena-platform
Agent: TestEngineer
Task: bootstrap RPS Arena platform
Context:
- Full node:test suite created for crypto, validation, game logic, services, and both storage backends; c8 enforces 100% coverage.
- CI via GitHub Actions (Node 20) runs npm ci + npm test; repo-wide pytest also executed with PYTHONPATH=src:. after changes.

Position:
- Coverage-first approach is working: both happy paths and error paths (invalid inputs, missing users, mismatched rounds, Mongo factory defaults) are exercised.
- In-memory store lets us avoid flaky external DB; MongoStore is tested with fakes and patched MongoClient to cover branch cases.

Recommendations:
- Keep adding targeted tests when new API endpoints or unlockable logic arrive; maintain c8 --100 threshold to prevent regressions.
- Add integration tests that drive HTTP endpoints (with in-memory store) to validate request parsing and static asset serving.
- When connecting to real Mongo, add smoke tests using test containers or a stubbed MongoClient to retain deterministic coverage.
